e `-$-1.95`. It now formats the absolute value and puts the sign in front, giving `-$3.10` and `-$0.05`.\n2. **`ledger/parse.py` – `parse_date`:** it returned `(year, day, month)` instead of `(year, month, day)`. This also broke `parse_record`.\n3. **`ledger/report.py` – `top_items`:** it sorted by total ascending and didn't break ties. It now sorts by total descending, then by item name ascending, as the docstring says.\n\n`parse_amount` already matched its docstring, so I left it alone.","ttft_ms":2483,"type":"result","duration_ms":17057,"uuid":"df5efd80-1764-4482-a2d6-ff3df67c0a42","ttft_stream_ms":851,"time_to_request_ms":27,"first_content_frame_ms":851,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
